# Copy to `.env` at the repo root and uncomment/adjust whatever you need.
# Anything left commented out uses the default from
# rinthel_tui/config.py::default_config(). The lines already uncommented
# here (CONTEXT_WINDOW, MTP_ENABLED, SCHED_ASYNC_CPU, CACHE_TYPE_K/V,
# MOE_CACHE_*) carry the values production actually runs with — verified
# 2026-09-24 against the live process; the config.py
# defaults differ and don't survive a real request on this hardware (see
# each section's comment). Production also overrides SPEC_TYPE,
# UBATCH/BATCH (2048), N_CPU_MOE (99), CACHE_REUSE (256), the fork paths
# and the vision toggle — shown commented below with their production value.
# `.env` is in .gitignore, never committed to the repo.

# ── LLAMA-SERVER (binary and model) ────────────────────────────
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_BIN=~/codacus/llama.cpp-perf-latest/build-cuda/bin/llama-server
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_MODEL_PATH=~/llama.cpp/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
# Vision projector (mmproj) — vacío/sin setear = sin visión, --mmproj se
# omite. F16 (899 MB) es la única cuantización que existe para este modelo
# en unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-GGUF (BF16/F32 son más grandes, no hay Q8).
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_MMPROJ_PATH=~/llama.cpp/models/mmproj-F16.gguf
# Toggle independiente del path — apaga/prende visión sin perder el path
# guardado. Default true; en false, --mmproj se omite aunque el path arriba
# esté seteado. También editable desde [N] CONFIGURAR > LLAMA-SERVER > VISIÓN.
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_MMPROJ_ENABLED=true
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_PORT=8080
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_LOG_PATH=~/Rinthel-general/logs/llama-server.log
# If false, [0] INSTALL/[1] BOOT/[2] RELOAD/[3] TERMINATE stop touching
# this service (won't install it, won't boot it, its badge won't show up).
# RINTHEL_LLAMA_ENABLED=true

# ── LLAMA-SERVER (inference flags) ─────────────────────────
# RINTHEL_NGL=all
#
# The uncommented values below deliberately differ from the hardcoded
# defaults in config.py — those defaults boot fine, but the default
# context (112000) dies on the first real request (~1024 prompt tokens)
# with CUDA error: out of memory, and the default batch 512 leaves a
# large part of the prefill throughput on the table. The values here are
# the config verified in production against 8 GB of VRAM (2026-09-24).
# Why each one is set this way: see docs/02-hardware-optimization.md.
RINTHEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
# RINTHEL_FLASH_ATTENTION=true
# RINTHEL_FIT_TO_MEMORY=false
# Production value: 99 = every MoE layer served from RAM, with the expert
# cache keeping the hot experts resident in VRAM (config.py default 60).
# RINTHEL_N_CPU_MOE=99
# RINTHEL_THREADS_BATCH=7
# RINTHEL_THREADS=8
# Production value: 2048 — the largest batch that still clears the
# ~300 MiB free-VRAM floor with the rest of this config (3072 crosses it).
# RINTHEL_UBATCH_SIZE=2048
# RINTHEL_BATCH_SIZE=2048
# RINTHEL_PARALLEL=1
# RINTHEL_TEMPERATURE=0.7
# RINTHEL_TOP_P=0.8
# RINTHEL_TOP_K=20
# RINTHEL_MIN_P=0.1
# RINTHEL_REPEAT_PENALTY=1.05
# No-op with this hybrid context (kv_unified=false): the server logs
# "cache_reuse is not supported by this context, it will be disabled" at
# every boot. Harmless, but it is NOT doing anything — don't count it as
# an active optimization. Production value shown.
# RINTHEL_CACHE_REUSE=256
# RINTHEL_CACHE_RAM=-1
# RINTHEL_LOAD_MODE=mlock
# ── MTP (multi-token prediction, speculative decoding) ─────────────────
# One switch turns it on/off: false = --spec-type none, true =
# --spec-type RINTHEL_SPEC_TYPE below. Same checkbox in [N] CONFIGURAR >
# LLAMA-SERVER > SPECULATIVE DECODING, so you never edit this file to
# toggle it. Costs ~650 MiB of VRAM for its compute buffer: on this 8 GB
# card, MTP + batch/ubatch 2048 reproduced a real CUDA OOM (48 MiB free,
# test-tarkAIrk/logs/27) — if the server dies on the first real request,
# drop RINTHEL_UBATCH_SIZE/RINTHEL_BATCH_SIZE to 1024 or 512 (512 is the
# minimum-VRAM candidate with MTP: KV q8_0 leaves 1270-1370 MiB free
# there, test-tarkAIrk/handoff/04) or turn MTP off again. MTP also does
# not support --parallel > 1 nor --mmproj (the latter is simply omitted
# from the command while MTP is on). Details:
# docs/02-hardware-optimization.md.
# Current state: OFF since 2026-09-24 (Tarkark's call — ~650 MiB-1 GB of
# VRAM for ~+6-7 gen_tps doesn't fit next to batch 2048).
RINTHEL_MTP_ENABLED=false
# Mode used while the switch above is on — draft-mtp is what the MTP-aware
# gguf (unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-GGUF) expects.
# RINTHEL_SPEC_TYPE=draft-mtp
# Draft depth per speculative round (higher = faster generation, more VRAM).
# RINTHEL_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=2
# true = llama.cpp's async CPU scheduling stays ON (no
# --no-sched-async-cpu flag in the command). Production value, verified
# 2026-09-24. Its isolated contribution to speed has never been measured;
# don't flip without a before/after run (docs/02-hardware-optimization.md).
RINTHEL_SCHED_ASYNC_CPU=true
# KV cache quantization (default f16 if left commented out). q8_0/q8_0
# roughly halves KV cache size — validated in production (agent-bench
# round, no quality/loop regression, min free VRAM 121-308 MiB → 1270-1370
# MiB under real load), see test-tarkAIrk/logs/22-2026-09-15-kv-cache-quant-q8-validacion-agentica.md.
# Always quantize both k and v together — one without the other silently
# overflows to shared PCIe memory, see test-tarkAIrk/handoff/01-gotchas.md.
RINTHEL_CACHE_TYPE_K=q8_0
RINTHEL_CACHE_TYPE_V=q8_0

# ── MOE TRACE / EXPERT CACHE ────────────────────────────────────
# RINTHEL_MOE_TRACE_BUILD=~/codacus/llama.cpp-perf-latest/build-cuda/bin/llama-moe-trace
# RINTHEL_MOE_TRACE_OUT_DIR=~/codacus/profiles
#
# The expert cache (--moe-cache-profile/--moe-cache-slots) is only added
# to the command if RINTHEL_MOE_CACHE_SLOTS > 0 (see
# rinthel_tui/lifecycle/services.py). +121% prefill speed over no cache;
# free VRAM under real load ends at ~700 MiB with the current batch/ubatch
# 2048 and KV q8_0 (1270-1370 MiB at batch 512) against a ~300 MiB floor —
# deliberate trade-off. Details: docs/02-hardware-optimization.md.
RINTHEL_MOE_CACHE_PROFILE=~/codacus/profiles/qwen3.6-fase2b-merged.csv
RINTHEL_MOE_CACHE_SLOTS=16

# ── UNDERSTORY (MCP memory layer) ──────────────────────────────
# Default: <repo>/understory (subtree, Fase 1 del monorepo) — ya no
# ~/understory-poc. Estado real (bundle) vive en <repo>/data/understory,
# fuera del subtree; ver docker-compose.yaml de la raíz.
# RINTHEL_UNDERSTORY_DIR=~/Rinthel-general/understory
# RINTHEL_UNDERSTORY_PORT=3800
# RINTHEL_UNDERSTORY_ENABLED=true

# ── PITHAGORAS (task portal) ───────────────────────────────────
# Default: <repo>/pithagoras (subtree) — ya no ~/pithagoras. Estado real
# (portal.db/sessions) vive en <repo>/data/pithagoras.
# RINTHEL_PITHAGORAS_DIR=~/Rinthel-general/pithagoras
# RINTHEL_PITHAGORAS_PORT=4100
# RINTHEL_PITHAGORAS_ENABLED=true

# ── UNDERSTORY + PITHAGORAS: secrets/env de docker-compose ─────────────
# Estos NO son RINTHEL_* (no los lee rinthel_tui/config.py) — los lee
# docker-compose.yaml directo, porque ahora corre desde la raíz con un solo
# .env en vez de uno por servicio. Ver docker-compose.yaml + AGENTS.md.
# AUTH_TOKEN=                    # understory, debe == UNDERSTORY_TOKEN
# UNDERSTORY_TOKEN=              # pithagoras -> mcp de understory
# PORTAL_PASSWORD=
# PORTAL_SECRET=                 # openssl rand -hex 32
# TS_AUTHKEY=                    # solo si usás el perfil "vpn" de tailscale
#
# Excepción a lo de arriba: OPENCODE_API_KEY SÍ tiene Field propio en
# rinthel_tui/config.py (pithagoras.opencode_api_key), así que además de
# leerla docker-compose la podés editar desde [N] CONFIGURAR. Es la key de
# OpenCode Zen que pi usa para los providers `opencode`/`opencode-go`
# (models: claude-*, gpt-5*, gemini-3*, deepseek-v4-flash-free, …). Vacía =
# esos modelos no aparecen en el picker del portal (SdkPiClient.getModels
# solo lista modelos con auth resoluble).
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=
#
# El fork de understory exige un LLM configurado para bootear (a diferencia
# de la imagen upstream vieja) — sin esto el contenedor crashea en loop con
# "No LLM configured". Mínimo funcional: apuntar al llama-server local vía
# host.docker.internal (ver extra_hosts en understory/docker-compose.yml).
# Stopgap de boot, no wiring real de Model provider (eso es Fase 4).
# LLM_API_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=local-no-auth
# LLM_API_FORMAT=openai
# LLM_MODEL=Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY compartida por Pithagoras (fallback provider) NO se le
# pasa a understory a propósito (ver comentario en understory/docker-
# compose.yml) — usar UNDERSTORY_OPENROUTER_API_KEY si understory necesita
# su propio OpenRouter más adelante.
# UNDERSTORY_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── TUI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Disables visual effects (glow/glitch/ripple) — useful in CI or slow terminals.
# RINTHEL_EFFECTS=true

# ── DAEMON (rinthel-daemon, proceso propio — no un servicio gestionado) ──
# Puerto donde escucha el daemon FastAPI. `rinthel-boot.sh` lo lee de acá
# para chequear si ya está arriba antes de autostartearlo, y para pasárselo
# al binario del cliente (`--port`).
# RINTHEL_DAEMON_PORT=8765

# ── RINTHEL HOST EXEC (daemon de ejecución en el host) ────────────
# Puerto del daemon nuevo (separado del de rinthel_tui). Default 8766 si
# no se setea.
# RINTHEL_HOSTEXECD_PORT=8766
# Token compartido entre la extensión de pi (dentro de Pithagoras) y el
# daemon (en el host) — generar con: openssl rand -hex 32
# RINTHEL_HOSTEXECD_TOKEN=

# ── INSTALL (infra bootstrap on a new machine, [0] INSTALL) ──
# RINTHEL_LLAMACPP_REPO_DIR=~/codacus/llama.cpp-perf-latest
# RINTHEL_LLAMACPP_REPO_URL=https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp.git
# RINTHEL_MODEL_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-GGUF/resolve/main/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
# RINTHEL_PITHAGORAS_REPO_URL=https://github.com/WilliamBarriga/pithagoras.git
# Folder Pithagoras mounts at /workspaces (WORKSPACES_DIR in its .env) —
# default $HOME.
# RINTHEL_WORKSPACES_DIR=~
